pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% `pbc` registers NO database proofgoals, so `proofgoal 1` used to FABRICATE the goal
% `C_1 | witness` with an empty witness -- i.e. `C_1` itself. The scope it opened therefore
% carried the premise `~C_1` while `C_1` was still in the database, so `rup >= 1 ;` was an
% instant meaningless contradiction, and closing the goal marked the ENCLOSING `pbc`
% obligation (a contradiction from `~C`) as discharged without ever checking it.
% Six lines, no arithmetic, and it forged `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` for `x1 OR x2`.
f 1 ;
pbc >= 1 : subproof
    proofgoal 1
        rup >= 1 ;
    qed;
qed;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
